{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CbAVc618ATCquE1B5bNAuA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for a Dream simulation based on the research context provided. Let me analyze the project carefully.\n\nKey context:\n- MVP results: F1=0.9055 on conf≥2 data, Repeat-3 baseline at 0.84\n- Core risks: (1) conf≥2 data might be too easy, full data generalization is key; (2) Repeat-3 at 0.84 is already strong; (3) weak supervision framework novelty; (4) EMNLP venue fit\n- Three claims: weak supervision framework, temporal modeling superiority, cross-agent transferability\n\n\n- Several critical experiments still need to run: full data generalization, LF oracle comparison, LLM-as-judge positioning, cross-agent transfer, gold set evaluation, and temporal modeling ablations\n- Best case has the probe generalizing well and outperforming baselines across the board; median case shows degradation but probe still competitive; worst case reveals significant F1 drops and weak transfer\n- I'm now defining specific metric thresholds for each tier to evaluate how these experiments actually perform Now I'm working through the performance scenarios across different data configurations. Looking at the full dataset of around 54,809 windows, I need to reconcile how the high-confidence subset (conf≥2 with ~15,401 windows at F1=0.9055) relates to the lower-confidence examples that make up the rest of the data.\n\nThe key tension is that conf=1 examples—which represent about 72% of the full dataset—come from single labeling function votes and introduce substantial noise. This matters because if the probe barely outperforms the Repeat-3 baseline on full data, it undermines the temporal modeling claim. Similarly, if cross-agent evaluation fails, that's a critical problem for the third claim.\n\nI'm now structuring the narrative scenarios carefully: the best case has all three claims holding strong as framed, while the median case requires softening some of the claims.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10123,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10123},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bad025c-838c-4ec2-ab4c-d67c1f87d4d3","uuid":"a0b84e6d-bbf7-46a8-99e0-02fd8a639350"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CbAVc618ATCquE1B5bNAuA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"全量数据泛化成功 + 跨agent迁移有效 + 人工标注验证通过——三条claims全部成立，原始framing无需调整\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - conf=1 噪声标签不显著损害probe学习能力，全量训练F1仅小幅下降\n      - GRU probe在全量数据上仍显著优于Repeat-3和LF oracle，证明时序建模捕获了LF规则之外的信号\n      - 跨agent迁移（SWE-agent→OpenHands）保持有效，F1绝对值可用\n      - 人工标注gold set确认majority vote标签质量≥80%，消除circular evaluation顾虑\n      - LLM-as-judge在可比F1下token开销高出2x+，cost-accuracy Pareto明确有利于probe\n      - Mean-pooling+LR显著低于GRU，确认时序建模的增量价值\n    number_ranges:\n      probe_fulldata_macro_f1: [0.85, 0.91]\n      gap_vs_repeat3_fulldata_pp: [5.0, 8.0]\n      gap_vs_lf_oracle_pp: [3.0, 7.0]\n      cross_agent_macro_f1: [0.78, 0.88]\n      human_gold_probe_f1: [0.82, 0.90]\n      human_label_accuracy_pct: [80, 90]\n      meanpool_lr_macro_f1: [0.72, 0.80]\n      llm_judge_f1: [0.82, 0.90]\n      llm_judge_cost_multiplier: [20, 100]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始framing完全成立。Headline: 弱监督框架成功迁移到agent trajectory领域，\n      GRU probe在全量噪声标签上学到了超越启发式规则的时序progress信号，\n      且跨实现可迁移。三条claims各有独立实验支撑，无需调整强度。\n      Paper结构：弱监督框架（方法论贡献）+ 时序建模实证（技术贡献）+ 跨agent泛化（泛化性贡献），\n      强调Snorkel到sequential trajectory的非平凡迁移 + 实用性（<5ms inference）。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"全量数据F1下降明显但仍优于baselines + 跨agent迁移部分成功 + 部分claims需降级调整\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - conf=1噪声导致全量训练F1下降5-10pp，但probe仍优于Repeat-3（gap缩小至2-5pp）\n      - Probe对LF oracle的优势收窄至边际显著，时序建模增量价值需要更精细的error analysis来论证\n      - 跨agent迁移F1下降明显（10-15pp），但仍优于random/majority baselines，模式可识别\n      - 人工标注揭示majority vote准确率在70-80%区间，conf=1子集标签质量成为明确弱点\n      - Mean-pooling+LR与GRU差距存在但不大（2-4pp），时序建模claim需补充attention可视化等定性证据\n    number_ranges:\n      probe_fulldata_macro_f1: [0.78, 0.85]\n      gap_vs_repeat3_fulldata_pp: [2.0, 5.0]\n      gap_vs_lf_oracle_pp: [1.0, 3.0]\n      cross_agent_macro_f1: [0.68, 0.78]\n      human_gold_probe_f1: [0.72, 0.82]\n      human_label_accuracy_pct: [70, 80]\n      meanpool_lr_macro_f1: [0.75, 0.82]\n      llm_judge_f1: [0.80, 0.88]\n      llm_judge_cost_multiplier: [15, 80]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claim 2（时序建模显著优于启发式）从\"显著优于\"降级为\"在噪声标签下仍具竞争优势\"，\n      强调probe的鲁棒性而非绝对性能优势。Claim 3（跨agent迁移）从\"保持有效\"调整为\n      \"zero-shot迁移存在但需domain adaptation\"，增加few-shot fine-tuning实验作为补充。\n      重心转移：弱监督框架（Claim 1）升格为主贡献，probe成为框架的一个下游验证。\n      补充实验：(a) confidence-aware training（用conf权重加权loss）试图恢复全量数据性能，\n      (b) error analysis深挖probe捕获的Repeat-3遗漏模式作为定性贡献，\n      (c) data scaling曲线展示标注效率。Paper叙事从\"probe很强\"转向\"弱监督框架使这类研究成为可能\"。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"全量数据泛化失败暴露conf≥2选择偏差 + probe增量价值存疑 + 需要根本性reframe但不降venue\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - 全量训练F1跌破0.78，conf≥2的高F1被确认为选择偏差（高conf=容易样本）\n      - Probe在全量数据上与LF oracle/Repeat-3无显著差异，时序建模claim不成立\n      - 跨agent迁移基本失败（F1<0.68），泛化性claim不成立\n      - 人工标注揭示majority vote准确率<70%，弱监督标签质量不足以支撑训练\n      - Mean-pooling+LR接近或匹配GRU性能，证伪时序建模的必要性\n      - 但LF分析本身揭示了有价值的stagnation pattern taxonomy\n    number_ranges:\n      probe_fulldata_macro_f1: [0.68, 0.78]\n      gap_vs_repeat3_fulldata_pp: [-1.0, 2.0]\n      gap_vs_lf_oracle_pp: [-2.0, 1.0]\n      cross_agent_macro_f1: [0.55, 0.68]\n      human_gold_probe_f1: [0.62, 0.72]\n      human_label_accuracy_pct: [60, 70]\n      meanpool_lr_macro_f1: [0.66, 0.77]\n      llm_judge_f1: [0.78, 0.88]\n      llm_judge_cost_multiplier: [10, 50]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始三条claims均无法按设计强度成立。Reframe策略——放弃\"probe优于一切\"的叙事，\n      转向empirical study framing：\"What Do Labeling Functions Reveal About Agent Stagnation?\"\n      核心贡献变为：(1) 首个大规模agent stagnation的弱监督标注框架和taxonomy，\n      LF temporal dynamics分析（哪些信号leading vs lagging）成为主要发现；\n      (2) 全量vs高conf的性能差异本身成为关于data programming在sequential data上\n      failure mode的实证贡献——conf-aware sample selection作为方法论发现；\n      (3) 负面结果（probe≈LF oracle）说明当前embedding+简单架构不足以超越\n      domain-specific规则，指出未来方向（更强的trajectory encoder, \n      hierarchical modeling）。LLM-as-judge对比仍可保留（cost argument不依赖probe绝对性能）。\n      仍投EMNLP，但叙事从\"我们的方法更好\"转向\"我们提出了框架+发现了关键insights\"，\n      走Findings track而非main conference如果必要。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10123,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10123},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bad025c-838c-4ec2-ab4c-d67c1f87d4d3","uuid":"599bc59a-4a9c-4b62-a427-6bea22b8876c"}
